167" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324484 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ac12c64fe5282c78ea926eec823cec6b66c8fad9f153c4191d39ba7751e90e25.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324484 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324484 1111 #uuid "522b40b1-df2b-51f0-a855-93f605907700" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324485 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/c959785ef067b41eba5e5ca5f0759acdd81c9f613c92854ba5937be6bced2c86.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324485 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324485 1111 #uuid "16c46ae3-7c85-5e04-8d9b-847d98efed69" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324486 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/fe57c0cc2d75729921eb46408e0e4a6932eba06c00034f2ec4c579c8c5627376.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324486 1111 #uuid "5d88b7b6-f8e5-5336-be0b-fde47a0f6ad9" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324487 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/9cb42cde56fcbea0c489742cab1448890728dab584395129b21794115b1e1298.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324487 1111 #uuid "f587d4b4-a011-5cef-9b83-486575f7f6cc" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324488 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/96817ea42e1d860db97d3ee6bca79e9a8b03a0fd413c87ebc5679f746da3166b.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324488 1111 #uuid "15141def-f6ab-58e6-9ea1-e7be74fd8a71" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324489 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324490 13194139534980 true] [17592186324489 1089 "q-119674" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324489 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534980 true] [17592186324489 1100 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}?$" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324489 1113 #uuid "6fa5ee8e-9f67-5df0-bf90-49308c053565" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324489 1145 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-1,-2),(2,-2)$ and $(2,2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-2)}=-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{(-1)}=4, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,-2)}=-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,2)}=-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/5e6b2df4680cea04cda42312659c76ba713a025150ebcc547dddc2a6501aebf3.png)" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324491 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324492 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324493 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324494 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324495 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324492 13194139534980 true] [17592186324490 1110 #uuid "a1fef5ae-62dd-5135-82ed-1d4341fba671" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324491 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/d48911eaffd88e249ef115a5511bff979ffa0f848ef8a1e8556db07ad273e41a.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324491 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324491 1111 #uuid "3d1fc060-2b67-5f50-9bff-a1dc120e2f76" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324492 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/5e6b2df4680cea04cda42312659c76ba713a025150ebcc547dddc2a6501aebf3.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324492 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324492 1111 #uuid "6c51bc5f-4a86-5a11-97cc-238d366b7d11" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324493 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/a0f75b52c741eca3322f4fe61009ba3c65e573f588edf9d3785019a1227f9769.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324493 1111 #uuid "1cbf9240-79aa-5034-bc20-640be147b835" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324494 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/4afe9527d6ff39ce7f5325a4a35ce5095d9bf0b1beb2fcde4de86a977bdac9e8.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324494 1111 #uuid "eef5024a-78a8-554e-b551-be382194ab74" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324495 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/c78c6d760cffb3dfb95233f9fc21dfea5a951371b056827885d1aa35469a458c.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324495 1111 #uuid "86b66809-84ea-55f0-b1a9-b56df4bd97f5" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324496 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324497 13194139534980 true] [17592186324496 1089 "q-119766" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324496 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534980 true] [17592186324496 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324496 1113 #uuid "02428a19-79c0-54a0-bd59-933e59271090" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324496 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=6xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324497 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324498 13194139534980 true] [17592186324497 1000 #edb/ref