eld is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324524 1113 #uuid "a59de227-7569-5036-a40a-476b213ce2eb" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324524 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x-2)^{2}(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/d836463631120853e05b3b5fb9e534822cf5611747a3eb17e22333901bfb8fd3.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324526 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324527 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324528 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324529 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324530 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324526 13194139534980 true] [17592186324525 1110 #uuid "da5d8795-39a4-5f85-b829-b6ff9dfe89bf" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324526 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324526 1111 #uuid "d2d8b810-ee16-55d2-9b9b-c421ab2ac297" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324527 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324527 1111 #uuid "320cc140-04b0-5fee-90bc-6f47239c594f" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324528 1034 "I only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324528 1111 #uuid "b7ceeaa6-8909-50bd-8e0b-b66b881cfcc9" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324529 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324529 1111 #uuid "cff34d04-2bef-5503-83a8-9e00ad0e5fda" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324530 1034 "II only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324530 1111 #uuid "609d26fc-8f06-5de3-832f-9b0a0729c0b6" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324531 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324532 13194139534980 true] [17592186324531 1089 "q-49811" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324531 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534980 true] [17592186324531 1100 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}?$" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324531 1113 #uuid "bc230845-92ae-5b4b-bdb5-703586364780" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324531 1145 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(1,2),(1,0),$ and $(-1,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,2)}=2(1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,0)}=2(1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}=2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-2)}=2(-1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}(-2)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/3dcb95f44f53f046c543d281038c0ac03fb14357cecdb7b96d5f41d33e9b0ed6.png)" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324533 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324534 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324535 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324536 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324537 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324534 13194139534980 true] [17592186324532 1110 #uuid "a214396c-2389-5681-800a-aa66ebb1a006" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324533 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/9bba5f86445177b9124813e85bf9294b7b566a029686f163c685663f5b352e30.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324533 1111 #uuid "448e3e3d-ce66-5a02-807a-7108d2818dac" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324534 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/3dcb95f44f53f046c543d281038c0ac03fb14357cecdb7b96d5f41d33e9b0ed6.pn