/differential/14044888/assets/3ddcc5784dc1fd60ba3c95ecda373678d00fc6c45e6b5e5655febcc130c37d95.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324542 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324542 1111 #uuid "9e6d8335-509a-5346-b0a7-7db4e2af08ab" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324543 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/327d6ae536cd6d76eff01387b51a4d2cc0522559d6ec6d02e3a86c2a3977f7b2.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324543 1111 #uuid "cf1909e1-91af-5de0-b3f4-2e07b75192fc" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324544 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e7e267508d68c1d4eeb31509a4a2957e120cecab920481ba6dc2b0fa1f84433b.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324544 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324544 1111 #uuid "17de6847-5e71-5f02-b67a-9978b2a76c2c" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324545 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324546 13194139534980 true] [17592186324545 1089 "q-80499" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324545 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534980 true] [17592186324545 1100 "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+2y}{4}?$" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324545 1113 #uuid "a02659d4-1cf7-5679-b691-6c43c4b6a900" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324545 1145 "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(4,-2),(2,1),$ and $(-1,3).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(4,-2)}=\\frac{4+2(-2)}{4}=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,1)}=\\frac{2+2(1)}{4}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=\\frac{-1+2(3)}{4}=\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\