 true] [17592186324553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324554 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324555 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324556 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324557 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324558 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324558 13194139534980 true] [17592186324553 1110 #uuid "a9b707c9-e47c-5add-a169-f6eccbcdc564" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324554 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/7670c9662fec950b45f2f939ed416590d278875b168caea9d7e5b70f7c8c6a9f.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324554 1111 #uuid "6c3f0144-5323-51e0-bf06-a958a1fda69c" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324555 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/bfd9789a91f680d5105d9081e51103ffba5e986fa4a96331cde06df6d0c42854.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324555 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324555 1111 #uuid "a0dc2983-6298-533f-b556-bfa8493fe7ef" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324556 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/631f9d7772354c6962f98e857371eac65d0fe36116bbae60dacd0db7ba01bc04.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324556 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324556 1111 #uuid "54acd6e4-e0a4-576e-ae22-bdb394baefb5" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324557 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/3edf063230f100455638fa25f28a4c5e59e2e54884d9e273724b76ae483aa0bc.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324557 1111 #uuid "c94a90c5-b415-5b4d-94e2-28d5f920132b" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324558 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/543365359599203eb6f9e8824f6e3b2987a1fec9121568dd7a9098bfc16870f1.png" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534980 true] [17592186324558 1111 #uuid "1d4dec99-0602-5cd5-a37e-9582b8d81e57" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324559 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324560 13194139534980 true] [17592186324559 1089 "q-97477" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324559 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534980 true] [17592186324559 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324559 1113 #uuid "69d9aef9-325a-5644-bfec-8ec831c2020d" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324559 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=-xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant." 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324561 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324562 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324563 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324564 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324565 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324565 13194139534980 true] [17592186324560 1110 #uuid "f4099eba-f208-5df9-84e3-d9718331e137" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324561 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324561 1111 #uuid "a5e82298-1404-5124-852f-cdaed09f250d" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324562 1034 "I only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324562 1111 #uuid "c6be1802-65aa-564a-9b3a-099c23b2398b" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324563 1034 "III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324563 1111 #uuid "ec25e4e6-2778-52d3-94e0-cb4de63c8b17" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324564 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 