n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant." 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324575 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324576 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324577 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324578 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324579 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324575 13194139534980 true] [17592186324574 1110 #uuid "98c30d2d-b036-5c2d-8a6e-4fbcd0750f04" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324575 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324575 1111 #uuid "3f9ac6b4-1eb7-5953-b69f-e0bab75c2bc4" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324576 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324576 1111 #uuid "8db20139-ef29-523c-a82a-f9d854047d68" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324577 1034 "I only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324577 1111 #uuid "21c900e3-5727-5d2a-a848-ee7f02b4ccb7" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324578 1034 "III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324578 1111 #uuid "499565f9-007d-5936-bd34-710fa288127a" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324579 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324579 1111 #uuid "64dd550e-4a4a-518b-a8d6-c2fed808d822" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324580 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324581 13194139534980 true] [17592186324580 1089 "q-97495" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324580 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534980 true] [17592186324580 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+2)(y+2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-2$ and $y>-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-2$ and $y>-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-2$ and $y<-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324580 1113 #uuid "4235049c-7cc2-5176-8c56-91624ea6b2f2" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324580 1145 "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x+2)(y+2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=-2$ or $y=-2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/7d225d82eee3043380eda76506b28e81aee06d42a232348b91b0d5ceb04f3318.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/bd9eedd3b8d82415e8f3126236f2e3a3b4e326a7072057bbd21406da92a08139.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $x>-2$ and $y>-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x<-2$ and $y>-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x<-2$ and $y<-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region." 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324582 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324583 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324584 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324585 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324586 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324583 13194139534980 true] [17592186324581 1110 #uuid "2bdd2a90-88c4-544c-b468-eb943fd08ab9" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324582 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324582 1111 #uuid "770864f4-c3d3-5d88-96b5-131ce1bec3a0" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324583 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324583 1111 #uuid "b7265f38-606f-596e-9c26-128f305fcd84" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324584 1034 "I only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324584 1111 #uuid "8b65d57c-7041-5c39-86b4-11038518e3c4" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324585 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324585 1111 #uuid "b04163d6-827b-59c5-a05e-d100ca89fa6a" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324586 1034 "II only" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534980 true] [17592186324586 1111 #uuid "c094514f-64b7-5499-9fb1-c2f85d3a561a" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324587 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324588 13194139534980 true] [17592186324587 1089 "q-98233" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324587 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534980 true] [17592186324587 1100 "Given that $f(x,y)$ varies with both $x$ and $y,$ which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)?$" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324587 1113 #uuid "69047027-7fd9-581d-a6dd-06bc079f6f80" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324587 1145 "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ae2c8de966219eb473c42fa809bfde49b52c7c88efaf83fc7ab0d602d734e722.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e243f3fb7515d9858599775ce0391f85f1de237f08380e1ec3b7403b1ecdbf53.png)" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324589 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324590 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324591 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324592 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324593 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1041 "selection" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324589 13194139534980 true] [17592186324588 1110 #uuid "3f5e91d6-7b03-535a-9b7c-caad50ff324a" 13194139534980 true] [17592186324589 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ae